The tools page is the developer edition's tools page
====================================================

Skills already come first here, but the section itself was not the same section: this edition kept its
own two-panel split and its own blurbs, while the developer edition groups by the manifest's `owner`
field into three libraries — what QuixiDesk ships, what the edition adds, and the agent's own Hermes
library — with a catch-all so a skill whose owner has no panel still appears instead of vanishing.

This is that section, taken across whole rather than approximated: the same owner grouping, the same
three panels in the same order, the same blurbs. It stays honest in this edition — no skill here is
filed `volkdude85`, because the published build does not ship the developer's working library — so the
middle panel is empty here and fills the moment a skill carries that owner.

The names are masked on the way to the screen, as before: the owner becomes "the user", everybody else
becomes "someone". `Max` is deliberately not mapped — it is a first name and also `Max: 250`, and the
reader redacts file bodies.

